IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-requirements.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10 (A company's directors), Chapter 1
-- (Appointment and removal of directors), "Requirement to have directors" and the start of "Appointment":
-- ss 154 to 156C, lines 2022-2089 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); no seat.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". The quote lines are copied from it by
-- srcrefs.py quote (through work/build.py) and checked by srcrefs.py check --strict.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE   the answer to the question the function's NAME asks.
--   JUST FALSE is used only where the text says no in its own words (a "means", an "if", an "unless", a flat
--   negative); each such branch carries -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the words quoted from the text.
--   NOTHING is "not covered": each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- BORROWED ANSWERS (PLAN.md section 4). The keel's and the other parts' answers arrive as INPUTS, named for the
-- section that gives them: "s 4(1) ... private company" (BOOLEAN suffices), "s 1173(1) ... officer" and
-- "s 1121 ... in default" (MAYBE BOOLEAN). This module imports coa-core only (see NOTES.md, "The brief and PLAN.md").
--
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements (the naming rule).

-- ---- Part 10, Chapter 1: Requirement to have directors -----------------------------------------------------

-- Section 154(1): the "private company" arrives as a fact (s 4(1) is the keel's: BOOLEAN suffices).
-- src:2025 | 154 Companies required to have directors
-- src:2026 | (1) A private company must have at least one director.
@ref s 154(1) Companies required to have directors (src:2025-2026)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors the company has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(1) the private company meets the requirement to have at least one director` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(1) the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company must have at least one director"
    ELSE IF `the number of directors the company has` AT LEAST 1
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have at least one director"

-- src:2027 | (2) A public company must have at least two directors.
@ref s 154(2) Companies required to have directors (src:2027)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors the company has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(2) the public company meets the requirement to have at least two directors` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must have at least two directors"
    ELSE IF `the number of directors the company has` AT LEAST 2
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have at least two directors"

-- ---- s 155: at least one director who is a natural person ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:2028 | 155 Companies required to have at least one director who is a natural person
-- src:2029 | (1) A company must have at least one director who is a natural person.
@ref s 155(1) Companies required to have at least one director who is a natural person (src:2028-2029)
GIVEN `the number of the company's directors who are natural persons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(1) the company meets the requirement to have at least one director who is a natural person` MEANS
    IF `the number of the company's directors who are natural persons` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have at least one director who is a natural person"

-- src:2030 | (2) This requirement is met if the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office.
@ref s 155(2) Requirement met by a natural person holding the office as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office (src:2030)
GIVEN `the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office of director is held by a natural person otherwise by virtue of an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(2) the requirement is met by the office of director being held by a natural person as a corporation sole or by virtue of an office` MEANS
    IF `the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole` OR `the office of director is held by a natural person otherwise by virtue of an office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This requirement is met if the office of director is held by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office"

-- ---- s 156: direction requiring company to make appointment -----------------------------------------------

-- src:2031 | 156 Direction requiring company to make appointment
-- src:2032 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State that a company is in breach of—
-- src:2033 | section 154 (requirements as to number of directors), or
-- src:2034 | section 155 (requirement to have at least one director who is a natural person),
-- src:2035 | the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under this section.
@ref s 156(1) Direction requiring company to make appointment (src:2031-2035)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 154` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 155` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 156` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 154` OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 155`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State that a company is in breach of"; the power is given on that appearance and the text does not say the Secretary of State may not otherwise (fork F4)

-- src:2036 | (2) The direction must specify—
-- src:2037 | (a) the statutory requirement the company appears to be in breach of,
-- src:2038 | (b) what the company must do in order to comply with the direction, and
-- src:2039 | (c) the period within which it must do so.
@ref s 156(2)(a)-(c) What the direction must specify (src:2036-2039)
GIVEN `the direction specifies the statutory requirement the company appears to be in breach of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies what the company must do in order to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies the period within which the company must do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(2) the direction specifies what the section requires it to specify` MEANS
    IF       `the direction specifies the statutory requirement the company appears to be in breach of`
         AND `the direction specifies what the company must do in order to comply with the direction`
         AND `the direction specifies the period within which the company must do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must specify— (a) the statutory requirement the company appears to be in breach of, (b) what the company must do in order to comply with the direction, and (c) the period within which it must do so."

-- "not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given": the
-- shortest and longest periods are one and three calendar months (daydate's `add months`, which clamps to the
-- last day of a shorter month); both ends are inside the permitted period.
-- src:2040 | That period must be not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given.
@ref s 156(2) The period specified in the direction (src:2040)
GIVEN `the day the direction is given` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period the direction specifies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(2) the period the direction specifies is not less than one month or more than three months after the day the direction is given` MEANS
    IF       `the last day of the period the direction specifies` AT LEAST (`add months` `the day the direction is given` 1)
         AND `the last day of the period the direction specifies` AT MOST (`add months` `the day the direction is given` 3)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That period must be not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given."

-- src:2041 | (3) The direction must also inform the company of the consequences of failing to comply.
@ref s 156(3) The direction must inform the company of the consequences (src:2041)
GIVEN `the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must also inform the company of the consequences of failing to comply."

-- s 156(4): "(a) making the necessary appointment or appointments, and (b) giving notice of them under section 167G,
-- before the end of the period specified in the direction". The period is one the direction sets (s 156(2)), so
-- the day it ends is an input.
-- src:2042 | (4) Where the company is in breach of section 154 or 155 it must comply with the direction by—
-- src:2043 | (a) making the necessary appointment or appointments, and
-- src:2044 | (b) giving notice of them under section 167G,
-- src:2045 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 156(4) Compliance with the direction where the company is in breach (src:2042-2045)
GIVEN `the company is in breach of section 154 or 155` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the necessary appointment or appointments were made before the end of the period specified in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of them under section 167G was given before the end of the period specified in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(4) the company has complied with the direction by making the appointments and giving notice of them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is in breach of section 154 or 155`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the company is in breach of section 154 or 155"; the subsection says nothing of a company not in breach (fork F5)
    ELSE IF       `the necessary appointment or appointments were made before the end of the period specified in the direction`
              AND `notice of them under section 167G was given before the end of the period specified in the direction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must comply with the direction by— (a) making the necessary appointment or appointments, and (b) giving notice of them under section 167G, before the end of the period specified in the direction"

-- s 156(4) as a regulative rule: the company's two duties, both within the period the direction specifies. The
-- number of days is the period the direction allows (an input); the clock counts days from the day the direction
-- is given. HENCE FULFILLED / LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE ... are the text's: "it must comply ... before the end
-- of the period"; the consequence of failing is stated in the direction itself (s 156(3)) and by s 156(6), (7).
-- src:2042 | (4) Where the company is in breach of section 154 or 155 it must comply with the direction by—
-- src:2043 | (a) making the necessary appointment or appointments, and
-- src:2044 | (b) giving notice of them under section 167G,
-- src:2045 | before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 156(4) The company's duties under the direction (regulative rule) (src:2042-2045)
GIVEN `the number of days the direction allows from the day it is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 156(4) the company's duty to comply with the direction` MEANS
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, `Secretary of State`, "make the necessary appointment or appointments"
     WITHIN `the number of days the direction allows from the day it is given`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the necessary appointment or appointments were not made before the end of the period specified in the direction")
    RAND
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, `Secretary of State`, "give notice of them under section 167G"
     WITHIN `the number of days the direction allows from the day it is given`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "notice under section 167G was not given before the end of the period specified in the direction")

-- src:2046 | (5) If the company has already made the necessary appointment or appointments (or so far as it has done so), it must comply with the direction by giving notice of them under section 167G before the end of the period specified in the direction.
@ref s 156(5) Compliance where the company has already made the appointments (src:2046)
GIVEN `the company has already made the necessary appointment or appointments, so far as it has done so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of them under section 167G was given before the end of the period specified in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(5) the company has complied with the direction by giving notice of the appointments already made` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has already made the necessary appointment or appointments, so far as it has done so`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company has already made the necessary appointment or appointments (or so far as it has done so)"; the subsection says nothing of a company that has not (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `notice of them under section 167G was given before the end of the period specified in the direction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must comply with the direction by giving notice of them under section 167G before the end of the period specified in the direction"

-- s 156(5A) is a flat negative about a duty under another section: compliance with the direction does not discharge it.
-- src:2047 | (5A) Nothing in subsection (4) or (5) affects the duty imposed by section 167G to give notice within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section.
@ref s 156(5A) The duty to give notice under section 167G is unaffected (src:2047)
`s 156(5A) complying with the direction discharges the duty under section 167G to give notice within the period in section 167G(6)` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (4) or (5) affects the duty imposed by section 167G to give notice within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section."

-- s 156(6): who commits the offence. "officer of the company" is s 1173(1) and "in default" is s 1121 (INPUTS, MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- src:2048 | (6) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2049 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 156(6)(a) Offence by the company (src:2048-2049)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with a direction under section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(6)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with a direction under section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by"

-- src:2048 | (6) If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2049 | (a) the company, and
-- src:2050 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:2051 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 156(6)(b) Offence by every officer of the company who is in default (src:2048-2051)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with a direction under section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(6)(b) the officer in default commits the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company failed to comply with a direction under section 156`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with a direction under this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer"
         OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default`
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; the person is not an officer (the person is an officer of the company)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1)
    WHERE
        `in default` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"; an officer who is not in default is outside the limit
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121

-- s 156(7): "(7) ... liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for
-- continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale" and then
-- (the rendering runs the two wordings together) "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard
-- scale". The text file shows both wordings; which is in force is not decided by the sources (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- This function is the first wording (one-tenth of level 5); the second wording is the function after it.
-- src:2052 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 156(7) Penalty for the offence (src:2052)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 156(7) the penalty for the offence, under the wording ending one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only "on summary conviction"

-- The scale in pounds is not in the Act (it is set by the sentencing legislation): the pounds are INPUTS.
DECLARE `s 156(7) standard scale in pounds` HAS
    `the statutory maximum in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `level 4 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `level 5 on the standard scale in pounds` IS A NUMBER

-- The second wording: "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale".
-- src:2052 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 156(7) Penalty for the offence, second wording (src:2052)
GIVEN scale IS A `s 156(7) standard scale in pounds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 156(7) the daily default fine limit in pounds under the wording one-tenth of the greater of 5000 pounds or level 4 on the standard scale` MEANS
    (IF scale's `level 4 on the standard scale in pounds` AT LEAST 5000
     THEN scale's `level 4 on the standard scale in pounds`
     ELSE 5000) DIVIDED BY 10

-- A fine limit in pounds, for the limits that occur in ss 154 to 204; "a fine without a stated limit" has no amount.
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      scale IS A `s 156(7) standard scale in pounds`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 156(7) the fine limit in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no limit
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` f
         THEN JUST (f TIMES scale's `the statutory maximum in pounds`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` n f
         THEN IF n EQUALS 5
              THEN JUST (f TIMES scale's `level 5 on the standard scale in pounds`)
              ELSE IF n EQUALS 4
                   THEN JUST (f TIMES scale's `level 4 on the standard scale in pounds`)
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the pounds a level stands for are not in the Act; only levels 4 and 5 are asked of the user
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` p THEN JUST p

-- ---- Appointment: s 156A: each director to be a natural person --------------------------------------------

-- s 156A(1) read with (2) and (5): "may not be appointed ... unless the person is a natural person". The function
-- says whether the subsection BARS the appointment: JUST TRUE = barred. "(2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit the
-- holding of the office of director by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office"
-- and "(5) This section has effect subject to section 156B (power to provide for exceptions ...)": regulations under
-- s 156B are outside the sources, so an appointment within one of them answers NOTHING.
-- src:2054 | 156A Each director to be a natural person
-- src:2055 | (1) A person may not be appointed a director of a company unless the person is a natural person.
-- src:2056 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit the holding of the office of director by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office.
-- src:2062 | (5) This section has effect subject to section 156B (power to provide for exceptions from requirement that each director be a natural person).
@ref s 156A(1), (2) and (5) Each director to be a natural person (src:2054-2056 and src:2062)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed to hold the office as a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one in which regulations under section 156B allow a person who is not a natural person to be appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(1) section 156A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not be appointed a director of a company unless the person is a natural person."
    ELSE IF `the person is appointed to hold the office as a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prohibit the holding of the office of director by a natural person as a corporation sole or otherwise by virtue of an office"
         ELSE IF `the case is one in which regulations under section 156B allow a person who is not a natural person to be appointed`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This section has effect subject to section 156B"; the regulations are not among the sources
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2057 | (3) An appointment made in contravention of this section is void.
@ref s 156A(3) An appointment in contravention is void (src:2057)
GIVEN `the answer under section 156A(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(3) the appointment made is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 156A(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appointment made in contravention of this section is void"; this section's bar does not apply, so it says nothing of the appointment
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the appointment contravenes the section turns on regulations under section 156B

-- src:2058 | (4) Nothing in this section affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts or any other enactment if the person—
-- src:2059 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2060 | (b) acts as shadow director,
-- src:2061 | although the person could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director.
@ref s 156A(4) Liability of a person who purports to act as director or acts as shadow director (src:2058-2061)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person could not, by virtue of section 156A, be validly appointed as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(4) section 156A leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as shadow director`) AND `the person could not, by virtue of section 156A, be validly appointed as a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as shadow director, although the person could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director"

-- src:2063 | (6) If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2064 | (a) the company purporting to make the appointment,
@ref s 156A(6)(a) Offence by the company purporting to make the appointment (src:2063-2064)
GIVEN `a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(6)(a) the company purporting to make the appointment commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by"

-- src:2063 | (6) If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2064 | (a) the company purporting to make the appointment,
-- src:2065 | (b) where the purported appointment is of a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, that body corporate or firm, and
@ref s 156A(6)(b) Offence by the body corporate or firm purportedly appointed (src:2063-2065)
GIVEN `a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purported appointment is of a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(6)(b) the body corporate or firm purportedly appointed commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF `the purported appointment is of a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the purported appointment is of a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, that body corporate or firm"

-- src:2063 | (6) If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2064 | (a) the company purporting to make the appointment,
-- src:2065 | (b) where the purported appointment is of a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, that body corporate or firm, and
-- src:2066 | (c) every officer of a person falling within paragraph (a) or (b) who is in default.
-- src:2067 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of a company.
@ref s 156A(6)(c) Offence by every officer in default of a person within (a) or (b) (src:2063-2067)
GIVEN `a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156A(6)(c) the officer in default commits the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a purported appointment is made in contravention of section 156A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a purported appointment is made in contravention of this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer"
         OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default`
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; the person is not an officer (the person is an officer of a person falling within paragraph (a) or (b))
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1)
    WHERE
        `in default` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"; an officer who is not in default is outside the limit
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121

-- s 156A(7): the penalty depends on where the person is convicted ("in England and Wales ... to a fine; in Scotland
-- or Northern Ireland ... level 5"); a conviction not placed in one of the three, or on indictment, is not covered.
-- src:2068 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:2069 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:2070 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 156A(7) Penalty for the offence (src:2068-2070)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 156A(7) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only on summary conviction in one of the three places

-- ---- s 156B (power to provide for exceptions) is machinery: no function; see NOTES.md (inert, reason 2). -------

-- ---- s 156C: existing director who is not a natural person ------------------------------------------------

-- "the day after the end of the period of 12 months beginning with the day on which section 156A comes into
-- force": a period of 12 months beginning with day C ends on the day before C's anniversary, so the relevant day
-- is C plus twelve months. The day section 156A comes into force is not in the Act's own text of these sections
-- (it is fixed by commencement provisions outside the sources): an INPUT.
-- src:2080 | 156C Existing director who is not a natural person
-- src:2081 | (1) In this section “the relevant day” is the day after the end of the period of 12 months beginning with the day on which section 156A comes into force.
@ref s 156C(1) The relevant day (src:2080-2081)
GIVEN `the day on which section 156A comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 156C(1) the relevant day` MEANS
    `add months` `the day on which section 156A comes into force` 12

-- src:2082 | (2) Where—
-- src:2083 | (a) a person appointed a director of a company before section 156A comes into force is not a natural person, and
-- src:2084 | (b) the case is not one excepted from that section by regulations under section 156B,
-- src:2085 | that person ceases to hold office by virtue of that appointment on the relevant day.
@ref s 156C(2) Existing director who is not a natural person ceases to hold office (src:2082-2085)
GIVEN `the day on which section 156A comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the person was appointed a director before section 156A comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is excepted from section 156A by regulations under section 156B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156C(2) the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of that appointment` MEANS
    IF       `the person was appointed a director before section 156A comes into force`
         AND `the person is not a natural person`
         AND NOT (`the case is excepted from section 156A by regulations under section 156B`)
    THEN IF `the day in question` AT LEAST (`s 156C(1) the relevant day` `the day on which section 156A comes into force`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person ceases to hold office by virtue of that appointment on the relevant day"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a person appointed a director of a company before section 156A comes into force is not a natural person, and (b) the case is not one excepted from that section by regulations under section 156B"

-- src:2086 | (2A) Nothing in this section affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts or any other enactment, if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (2), the person—
-- src:2087 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2088 | (b) acts as shadow director.
@ref s 156C(2A) Liability of a person who has ceased to hold office (src:2086-2088)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156C(2A) section 156C leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (2)` AND (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as shadow director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (2), the person— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as shadow director"

-- s 156C(3) addresses the registrar: what it means for the company and its directors is that a note will appear in
-- the register recording that notice of a person's ceasing to be a director was not given.
-- src:2089 | (3) If it appears to the registrar that, as a result of subsection (2), a company should have given notice under section 167G of a person having ceased to be a director but has failed to do so, the registrar must include a note in the register recording that fact.
@ref s 156C(3) The registrar must note the failure to give notice (src:2089)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that, as a result of subsection (2), the company should have given notice under section 167G of a person having ceased to be a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to give that notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156C(3) the registrar must include a note in the register recording that the company failed to give notice` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the registrar that, as a result of subsection (2), the company should have given notice under section 167G of a person having ceased to be a director` AND `the company has failed to give that notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the registrar that, as a result of subsection (2), a company should have given notice under section 167G of a person having ceased to be a director but has failed to do so"
